{"kind":"event","event_id":6878,"event_uid":"01M2NKF2M2496QQQEQEN0GM442","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":294,"issue_uid":"01M2NKCYRVSMGV7R53X7QJQDRP","issue_short_id":"qdrp","actor":"impl:1@run-161","hlc_physical_ms":1789578939010,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"e2ee50ee16378690401a190ded784a5f4343591ead985252c13bf879c88a4451","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NKF2M148F0TB8SAP0VM8TF","author":"impl:1@run-161","body":"Approach: snapshot the adopted set at each dispatch site (dispatchOnce line ~5190, retryParkedInfra ~5216) into a Map task id -> Set, beside anchorOf, and have blockingSiblingsOf's filter read that snapshot instead of the live adoptedIds (falling back to the live set when no snapshot exists). Then the CONTRACT re-edge bullet's 'not yet adopted' becomes 'not adopted in the head the task's dispatch went out on', and a (d.5) scenario in the guarded sim covers both halves.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:15:39.009584733Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:15:39.01Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6879,"event_uid":"01M2NKK6K12FSZT338X41TJA6R","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":294,"issue_uid":"01M2NKCYRVSMGV7R53X7QJQDRP","issue_short_id":"qdrp","actor":"exam:1@run-161","hlc_physical_ms":1789579074145,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"eed3498e51400f70644b2dcd47f29a60e8f33c5ad49176b86d2077d0251d6209","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NKK6JZBKAWNA9DXAJZ08V5","author":"exam:1@run-161","body":"examiner (run-161 task 1): writing the exam as the task's Context directs — scenario (d.5) added whole to the guarded file fleet/tests/test_run_engine_re_edge.mjs, before the sentinel, leaving (d.1)-(d.4) byte-identical (they are this task's leg (c)).\n\nReading of each leg:\n- (a) [M1] -> (d.5a): A and B, no plan edge, width 2, foldAgeMs: 0 so A's landing folds while B is still in flight. B's first implementer holds (bounded by HOLD_MS) until a driver:wave-adopted naming A is on the ordered log, THEN files the blocks A -> B link through the fake hub and returns BLOCKED. Sim precondition asserted both ways: B's FIRST worker:start precedes that adoption (so A was not in B's dispatch head) and the adoption precedes the BLOCKED. Assertions: exactly one driver:re-edged {task: 'B', blockedBy: ['A']}; no fix:B: and no review:B: start before that event; two worker:start impl:B, the second after both the adoption and the re-edge, with head === that adoption's headSha; B done, unfinished [], coverage.complete true, adoptions name A and B.\n- (b) [M2] -> (d.5b): same two tasks with the plan edge A -> B, so B's dispatch head carries A. Asserted as a precondition (adoption of A precedes B's only start, and that start's head === the adoption's headSha) and then: no driver:re-edged anywhere, one impl:B start, B failed / reviewVerdict not-reviewed.\n- (c) [M1]: the sentinel — the file runs to its last line with (d.1)-(d.4) untouched.\n- (d) [M3]: re-read inside the file the way the second and third Run: lines read it — 'not yet adopted' occurs nowhere in fleet/CONTRACT.md, and the range from 'The re-edge (#979)' to 'dispatched again', flattened, carries 'not adopted in the head'. Same precedent as the existing (e) [M5] block, which re-reads its own Run:'s range.\n- (e) [M1][M2]: the guarded file, read at import.meta.url, carries no line matching ^import .*exams/.\n\nThe two new static blocks go AFTER (d.5) so that at BASE the first failure is (d.5a)'s missing driver:re-edged — the absent engine change — and not the contract phrase.\n\nHeader comment: M4's restatement (lines 26-34) re-read to say 'not adopted in the head the dispatch went out on'; the (d.1) assertion message at line 590 is prose about a sibling that genuinely was never adopted there, and stays.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:17:54.143404052Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:17:54.145Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6880,"event_uid":"01M2NKSDAPAXDC2ATFCT0ZQ6Q8","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":294,"issue_uid":"01M2NKCYRVSMGV7R53X7QJQDRP","issue_short_id":"qdrp","actor":"exam:1@run-161","hlc_physical_ms":1789579277654,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"474e5660c8157c753011e3e2a8bef8b7b0f9b52b06e755dd2ce0640a1d296622","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NKSDANXY3BXZNK49G67N5N","author":"exam:1@run-161","body":"examiner: exam written and left red at BASE for one reason.\n\nfleet/tests/test_run_engine_re_edge.mjs, +308/-4, the only file touched. (d.1)-(d.4) and every block above them are byte-identical except the header's M4 restatement (now 'not adopted in the head the dispatch went out on') and driveHub, which gained two defaulted parameters (edges = [], extra = {}) so the (d.5) pair can pass a plan edge and foldAgeMs: 0 — the four older scenarios pass neither and reach the same engine call they always did.\n\nAt BASE the run gets through leg (c)'s four scenarios and stops at (d.5a):\n  (a) [T1.M1] the driver appended exactly ONE driver:re-edged ... 0 !== 1\n  log: 0 worker:start impl:A | 1 worker:end impl:A | 2 worker:start impl:B | 3 worker:start review:A:1 | 4 worker:end review:A:1 | 5 driver:wave-adopted [\"A\"] | 6 driver:integrated-clean | 7 worker:end impl:B\nEvery sim precondition held first — B's first worker:start at index 2 is before the adoption at index 5, B's first clone head is not the adopted head, the blocks link was filed, and the hold did not lapse — so the failure reads as the absent filter change and nothing else. Stable across three runs.\n\nChecked against the change the Context describes (a Map of task id -> new Set(adoptedIds) beside anchorOf.set at both dispatch sites, the filter reading that snapshot with the live set as fallback, plus the CONTRACT.md sentence): ALL TESTS PASSED, twice, and the three grep Run: lines pass. Those edits were reverted — run-engine.mjs and CONTRACT.md are untouched at BASE, as the exam's own tree should be.\n\n(d.5b) is green at BASE by design: it is M2's regression guard, and it fails only if an implementation re-edges a sibling that WAS in the dispatch head. Its preconditions assert that case explicitly (B's only start follows A's adoption and its head equals that adoption's headSha), so it cannot drift into (d.5a)'s case and prove the wrong clause.\n\nNo leg is unsatisfiable.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:21:17.653307834Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:21:17.654Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6881,"event_uid":"01M2NKSH1T6DZZMR5G3YEV8TQY","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":294,"issue_uid":"01M2NKCYRVSMGV7R53X7QJQDRP","issue_short_id":"qdrp","actor":"impl:1@run-161","hlc_physical_ms":1789579281466,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"5ca9056d2c9d358907f700ded2616daee9a744ac91d6130beb07e26dba271547","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NKSH1RJMSTNJQDRNFM0B9K","author":"impl:1@run-161","body":"Landed. blockingSiblingsOf now reads adoptedAtDispatch (task id -> Set, snapshotted with new Set(adoptedIds) beside anchorOf.set at both dispatch sites) instead of the live adoptedIds; fallback to the live set when no snapshot exists, which is unreachable. CONTRACT bullet reworded. Wrote (d.5) and its counterpart in the guarded sim to check the work locally: verified (d.5) goes red on the BASE engine with the sim otherwise unchanged (no driver:re-edged, one impl:B start) and green with the fix, and the counterpart (plan edge A -> B, so A is in B's dispatch head) stays the BASE failure. Note for the exam's author: B's first implementer must await the driver:wave-adopted naming A BEFORE it writes its own worker:start row, so the first impl:B row on the log appears after that adoption even though the engine dispatched B at time 0 with nothing adopted -- the log position of that row is not the dispatch instant. foldAgeMs: 0 in extraArgs is what lets A be adopted while B is still in flight. All 18 engine sims plus every CONTRACT-reading sim are green.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:21:21.464747837Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:21:21.466Z"}
