{"kind":"event","event_id":6912,"event_uid":"01M2NM00A9SSW9ZFWJTYQ0K0HT","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":294,"issue_uid":"01M2NKCYRVSMGV7R53X7QJQDRP","issue_short_id":"qdrp","actor":"engine:run-161","hlc_physical_ms":1789579493705,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"aaab8e9d073e7be8cc58a16978748278cb5f0a8ff694b5f3fb4bdbc9b8dab049","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NM00A7T26RWQE11C25EPHV","author":"engine:run-161","body":"{\"kind\":\"driver:finding\",\"task\":\"1\",\"round\":1,\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"actor\":\"implementer\",\"detail\":\"fleet/run-engine.mjs: the dispatch snapshot is taken at a later instant than the head it claims to describe, so it can name a sibling whose work is not in the tree the worker was handed — the exact case M1 exists to re-edge. In `dispatchOnce` `head` is read at the top (`const head = adoptedHead`), but `adoptedAtDispatch.set(task.id, new Set(adoptedIds))` runs only after `await anchorClone(task, head)` (git fetch + detached checkout + `resetTaskClone` + the bootstrap command) and the optional `resetTaskClone` for a re-edged task. `foldEpoch` assigns `adoptedHead = merge.headSha` and `for (const t of epochTasks) adoptedIds.add(t.id)` on adjacent lines, and it runs on another lane under `underFoldLock`, which `anchorClone` does not hold — so a fold completing inside that window adds sibling S to `adoptedIds` while this dispatch's `head` still predates S. The worker is handed `head` (`runTask(task, head, siblingsNow(task))`), which lacks S's work; it returns BLOCKED naming S; `blockingSiblingsOf` reads `adoptedThen`, finds S present, filters it out, and the task ends `failed: not-reviewed` instead of being re-edged. `retryParkedInfra` has the identical skew (`head` at its top, snapshot after `anchorClone` and `resetTaskClone`). The added comment asserts the invariant the placement does not hold: \\\"task id → the ids IN that head\\\". The window is not theoretical — `anchorClone` is seconds of git and bootstrap IO and folds run concurrently on other lanes at width ≥ 2. Fix is to read the set in the same tick as `head`, which is the only instant at which `adoptedHead` and `adoptedIds` are consistent; both sites are inside this task's FILES. The exam does not catch this because (d.5a) adopts A strictly after B's `worker:start` is already on the log, i.e. after the snapshot was taken.\",\"paths\":[\"fleet/CONTRACT.md\",\"fleet/run-engine.mjs\",\"fleet/tests/test_run_engine_re_edge.mjs\"],\"evidence\":{\"read\":\"fleet/run-engine.mjs: the dispatch snapshot is taken at a later instant than the head it claims to describe, so it can name a sibling whose work is not in the tree the worker was handed — the exact case M1 exists to re-edge. In `dispatchOnce` `head` is read at the top (`const head = adoptedHead`), but `adoptedAtDispatch.set(task.id, new Set(adoptedIds))` runs only after `await anchorClone(task, head)` (git fetch + detached checkout + `resetTaskClone` + the bootstrap command) and the optional `r…\",\"against\":\"review round 1 of d8b207033431c6a1d2ce46c9596267aedf4eb623\"},\"id\":\"01M2NM007W0000S771HFD1CPMN\",\"ts\":1789579493628}","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:24:53.703458287Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:24:53.705Z"}
